---
// Zone diagram for the UniFi migration post: one box per network, default deny
// between zones, arrows only for the main deliberate exceptions. Static SVG,
// themed through the site tokens; Work is the one --signal element.
---

<figure class="zone-map">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 420 420" role="img" aria-labelledby="zm-title zm-desc">
    <title id="zm-title">Firewall zones and their exceptions</title>
    <desc id="zm-desc">
      Eleven networks, each its own firewall zone. Trusted and the admin VPN have
      admin access to every network. Home Assistant on Servers and the IoT network
      reach each other, and IoT uses DNS on Servers. DMZ reaches DNS and one app on
      Servers. Hypervisors reach storage on Servers, and the Mac mini on Servers has
      admin access back. The work laptop on the Work network reaches two hosts on
      Servers. The work VPN is walled off. Management, Lab and Guest have no
      exceptions drawn.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="zm-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" class="zm-head" />
      </marker>
      <marker id="zm-arrow-signal" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" class="zm-head-signal" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- Admin tier -->
    <rect x="10" y="12" width="190" height="40" rx="3" class="zm-box" />
    <text x="105" y="37" class="zm-name">Trusted</text>
    <rect x="220" y="12" width="190" height="40" rx="3" class="zm-box" />
    <text x="315" y="37" class="zm-name">Admin VPN</text>

    <text x="210" y="74" class="zm-label">admin access to every network</text>
    <line x1="58" y1="82" x2="362" y2="82" class="zm-line" />
    <line x1="58" y1="82" x2="58" y2="99" class="zm-line" marker-end="url(#zm-arrow)" />
    <line x1="210" y1="82" x2="210" y2="99" class="zm-line" marker-end="url(#zm-arrow)" />
    <line x1="362" y1="82" x2="362" y2="99" class="zm-line" marker-end="url(#zm-arrow)" />

    <!-- Row B -->
    <rect x="10" y="102" width="96" height="40" rx="3" class="zm-box" />
    <text x="58" y="127" class="zm-name">Management</text>
    <rect x="162" y="102" width="96" height="40" rx="3" class="zm-box" />
    <text x="210" y="127" class="zm-name">Hypervisors</text>
    <rect x="314" y="102" width="96" height="40" rx="3" class="zm-box" />
    <text x="362" y="127" class="zm-name">Lab</text>

    <!-- Hypervisors <-> Servers -->
    <line x1="196" y1="146" x2="196" y2="202" class="zm-line" marker-end="url(#zm-arrow)" />
    <text x="188" y="178" class="zm-label zm-end">storage</text>
    <line x1="224" y1="202" x2="224" y2="146" class="zm-line zm-dash" marker-end="url(#zm-arrow)" />
    <text x="232" y="178" class="zm-label zm-start">Mac mini: admin</text>

    <!-- Row C -->
    <rect x="10" y="206" width="96" height="40" rx="3" class="zm-box" />
    <text x="58" y="231" class="zm-name">IoT</text>
    <rect x="162" y="206" width="96" height="40" rx="3" class="zm-box" />
    <text x="210" y="231" class="zm-name">Servers</text>
    <rect x="314" y="206" width="96" height="40" rx="3" class="zm-box" />
    <text x="362" y="231" class="zm-name">DMZ</text>

    <line x1="110" y1="226" x2="158" y2="226" class="zm-line" marker-start="url(#zm-arrow)" marker-end="url(#zm-arrow)" />
    <text x="134" y="219" class="zm-label">HA</text>
    <text x="134" y="241" class="zm-label">DNS</text>
    <line x1="310" y1="226" x2="262" y2="226" class="zm-line" marker-end="url(#zm-arrow)" />
    <text x="286" y="219" class="zm-label">DNS,</text>
    <text x="286" y="241" class="zm-label">1 app</text>

    <!-- Work -> Servers, the post's argument -->
    <line x1="210" y1="306" x2="210" y2="250" class="zm-line zm-signal" marker-end="url(#zm-arrow-signal)" />
    <text x="218" y="282" class="zm-label zm-start zm-signal-text">laptop: 2 hosts</text>

    <!-- Row D -->
    <rect x="10" y="310" width="96" height="40" rx="3" class="zm-box" />
    <text x="58" y="335" class="zm-name">Guest</text>
    <rect x="162" y="310" width="96" height="40" rx="3" class="zm-box zm-signal-box" />
    <text x="210" y="335" class="zm-name zm-signal-text">Work</text>
    <rect x="314" y="310" width="96" height="40" rx="3" class="zm-box zm-dash" />
    <text x="362" y="328" class="zm-name">Work VPN</text>
    <text x="362" y="343" class="zm-label">walled off</text>

    <text x="210" y="388" class="zm-label">No arrow: denied.</text>
    <text x="210" y="406" class="zm-label">Each network is its own zone.</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    Traffic between zones is denied unless an arrow says otherwise. These are the
    main exceptions, not every rule. Work, highlighted, is the two-device network
    this post defends.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .zone-map {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    max-width: 34rem;
  }
  .zone-map svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    color: var(--paper);
  }
  .zone-map figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }
  .zm-box {
    fill: var(--ink-2);
    stroke: var(--muted);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .zm-signal-box {
    stroke: var(--signal);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .zm-dash {
    stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  }
  .zm-name,
  .zm-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-anchor: middle;
    fill: currentColor;
  }
  .zm-name {
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .zm-label {
    font-size: 11.5px;
    fill: var(--muted);
  }
  .zm-start {
    text-anchor: start;
  }
  .zm-end {
    text-anchor: end;
  }
  .zm-signal-text {
    fill: var(--signal);
  }
  .zm-line {
    stroke: var(--muted);
    stroke-width: 1.25;
    fill: none;
  }
  .zm-signal {
    stroke: var(--signal);
    stroke-width: 1.75;
  }
  .zm-head {
    fill: var(--muted);
  }
  .zm-head-signal {
    fill: var(--signal);
  }
</style>
